419: There is no unrecorded mirror sign in this comparison. In the local
420: coordinates of F9 the circle-first orbit orientation is
421: \(-\Omega_{\rm source}\wedge d\gamma\). Thus the local seven-ball
422: orientation is the negative of complex \((X,y,\rho)\) followed by the
423: increasing height. The positive Hopf meridian is reversed at the same
424: time relative to that raw complex-plus-height normal orientation.
425: Changing both the six-dimensional orientation and the Euler class
426: leaves \((4x^3-p_1x)/24\) unchanged. This gives (SC.18) with the
427: positive height ordering in SC.3 and the positive \(\rho\)-loop of
428: F54.
429: 
430: The direct local calculation F55 gives \(H(e)=1\). Equations
431: (SC.17)--(SC.18), after the actual line and collar maps above, therefore
432: give the proposed oriented source-return value \(A=1\) and class
433: \(1\in\Theta_7\) in the run's Eells--Kuiper normalization. This final
434: promotion awaits independent audit of the full ambient, Hopf-line and
435: excision comparison in SC.3--SC.5; it is not an inference from the
436: weighted compact pencil's numerical invariants.
437: 
438: Exact symbolic identities and the integral plumbing certificate are
439: saved separately in `code/part3/source_cusp_trace.py` and its outputs.
